speechtext:
Mr. Campbell was appointed postmaster at Macleod on the 1st of January, 1885 ; his salary was $800 a year. He has been also acting as sheriff and his duties as sheriff interfered with the proper discharge of his duties of his office as postmaster and for that reason a change was made. On the 6th instant Mr. Samuel Heap was appointed in his place.
COMMISSION ON CAPITAL AND LABOUR ;
1886.

Mr. PORTER asked ;
1.	Was a chanter ever granted to the Rath-bun Company, or any other company or persons, to build a line of railway from Napanee to Deseronto, and locating the line of such railway along the bank of the Napanee river ? If so, when ?
2.	Has any Act been passed or charter granted to the Rath-bun Company, or any other person or company, to construct a line of railway from Napanee to Deseronto, changing the original location referred tio in paragraph one of this question, or authorizing any other location ? If so. when, and what location was ao authorized ?
